Think: For each path in file_list.csv, count lines and write "full_path,line_count" to per_file_line_counts.csv; record unreadable files to errors.log. I'll run a single awk command that executes wc -l for each path and handles errors.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F, '{
  path=$1;
  cmd = "wc -l < \"" path "\" 2>/dev/null";
  cnt = "";
  if ((cmd | getline cnt) <= 0) { close(cmd) } else { close(cmd) }
  if (cnt == "") {
    print path > "temp_workspace/errors.log";
    print path ",ERROR";
  } else {
    sub(/ .*/,"",cnt);
    print path "," cnt;
  }
}' temp_workspace/file_list.csv > temp_workspace/per_file_line_counts.csv
```

